[259.458661, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Report: Host `rdp-prod-01`  \n\n## 1. Executive Summary & Attack Chain\nAn external threat actor successfully compromised host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) via RDP credential brute forcing. The RDP service was exposed to the internet with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following initial access, the actor established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed a ransomware binary that encrypts files to `.locked` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`), initiated C2 communications and cryptocurrency mining (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`), and cleared the Security Event Log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\n\nWhile security product alerting (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the ransomware binary, scheduled task, and service, it **failed to detect** the Registry Run key persistence (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) and the cleared Security log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping\n\n| ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Tactic | Evidence / Finding | Alert Status | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **T1110** | Brute Force | Credential Access | External RDP brute force attack | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11` |\n| **T1021.001** | Remote Desktop Protocol | Lateral Movement | RDP logon allowed without NLA | Alerted | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` |\n| **T1059.001** | PowerShell | Execution | Execution of PowerShell post-compromise scripts | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` |\n| **T1486** | Data Encrypted for Impact | Impact | Ransomware `svc.exe` encrypts user files to `.locked` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |\n| **T1053.005** | Scheduled Task | Execution / Persistence | Scheduled task `UpdateHelper` runs `svc.exe` every 5 min | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` |\n| **T1547.001** | Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder | Persistence | Run key `svc -> C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\svc.exe` | **SILENT** | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\n| **T1543.003** | Windows Service | Persistence | Service `svc-helper` / `svc-helper.sys` installed | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` |\n| **T1070.001** | Clear Windows Event Logs | Defense Evasion | Security event log cleared (`EventID 1102`) | **SILENT** | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Threat Actor Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n- **Origin / Attacker IP**: `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-rdp[.]example[.]cn` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\n- **Crypto Mining Pool**: `stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]rdp[.]evil[:]3333` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)\n- **Crypto Wallet**: `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Evidence Artifacts & File Hashes\n\n1. **Ransomware Executable**:\n   - Path: `/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`)\n   - SHA256: `4f8a5c4380a18bca293c7e9130caf957973cc733e9b2c32c2e5240aa9e2c2dae`\n   - Description: Ransomware payload dropped in Public folder.\n2. **Scheduled Task**:\n   - Path: `/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`)\n   - SHA256: `2c2313138723024ae31eb2d8c399cc3f47ffd7221937f098247629dba83d730d`\n   - Description: `schtasks` task triggering `svc.exe` execution every 5 minutes.\n3. **Malicious Service Driver**:\n   - Path: `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)\n   - SHA256: `8525c122105c20ecbf866f40d8d60ad1fbbe21fd07a6b77c79182631931ede86`\n   - Description: Boot-start service driver supporting persistence and mining operations. Correlated with Event ID 7045 in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`.\n4. **Registry Run Key Persistence (Silent)**:\n   - Hive Path: `/Windo"]
[259.458697, "i", "ws/System32/config/SOFTWARE` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`)\n   - SHA256: `b08f4418b698c040964ae535a0ed3ea9c7b2ca83ffb0d32bd5c536c63e3c4971`\n   - Entry: `HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\\svc` -> `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe`\n5. **Cleared Security Event Log (Silent)**:\n   - Path: `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`)\n   - SHA256: `0d060e5e7946a8ba3d4853a8feb8f12660d8fec11898aa2903a7be2cede9da1b`\n   - Event: Event ID 1102 indicating Security event log was cleared by attacker to destroy audit trail.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security Telemetry & Gap Analysis\n\nThe SAS alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json`) covered three threat items:\n- `ALERT-01`: Ransomware binary (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`)\n- `ALERT-02`: Scheduled task (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`)\n- `ALERT-03`: Malicious service (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)\n- `ALERT-04`: RDP baseline weakness (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`)\n\n**Coverage Gaps Identified**:\n1. **Registry Run Key Persistence**: Present in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` but missing from security alerts.\n2. **Event Log Cleared Anti-Forensics**: Present in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` (Event ID 1102) but missing from security alerts.\nEOF\n"]
