[304.29529, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan: Host `rdp-prod-01`  \n\n## 1. Plan Overview & Principles\nThis remediation plan outlines containment, eradication, baseline hardening, and recovery actions for host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). In accordance with incident response rules:\n- **Quarantine / Backup Over Deletion**: Malware samples, persistence artifacts, and modified configurations are backed up or quarantined rather than immediately deleted to preserve evidence.\n- **Evidence-Based Actions**: Every action is mapped directly to forensic evidence from `/disk` or `/sas`.\n- **Change Ticket Reconciliation**: Reconciles draft ticket `CHG-9792` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-9792\n\n| # | Action | Target / Location | Status | Rationale & Evidence | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | Block inbound network traffic | IP `198.51.100.92` | **PROPOSED** | Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with confirmed threat actor IP `198.51.100.92`. | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` |\n| **2** | Enable NLA & Harden RDP | TCP Port 3389 / RDP | **PROPOSED** | Entry was via RDP password brute force (`T1110`), enabled by NLA being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`). Corrected from invalid BlueKeep claim. | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` |\n| **3** | Cancel cron miner removal | `/var/spool/cron/root` | **REJECTED** | Target host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`); Linux cron miner was a stale/erroneous draft entry. | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\n| **4** | Quarantine ransomware binary | `/Users/Public/svc.exe` | **TODO** | Move `svc.exe` (`4f8a5c4380a18bca293c7e9130caf957973cc733e9b2c32c2e5240aa9e2c2dae`) to secure forensic quarantine folder. | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |\n| **5** | Disable & Quarantine Scheduled Task | `/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` | **TODO** | Backup task definition XML and remove `UpdateHelper` task that executes `svc.exe` every 5 minutes. | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` |\n| **6** | Quarantine Registry Run Key | `/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` | **TODO** | Delete Registry Run value `svc -> C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\svc.exe` under `HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Run`. (**Silent finding**) | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\n| **7** | Stop & Disable Malicious Service | `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` | **TODO** | Stop service `svc-helper`, set startup type to Disabled, and move driver `svc-helper.sys` (`8525c122105c20ecbf866f40d8d60ad1fbbe21fd07a6b77c79182631931ede86`) to quarantine. | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` |\n| **8** | Restore Audit Policy & Centralized Logging | `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` | **TODO** | Security event log was wiped (`EventID 1102`). Re-enable security auditing and configure SIEM log forwarding. (**Silent finding**) | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Step-by-Step Execution & Verification Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment\n1. **Perimeter Firewall Rule**: Add inbound drop rule for `198.51.100.92` on perimeter firewall (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).\n   - *Verification*: Attempt ICMP/TCP connections from test subnets to verify blocking.\n2. **Isolate Host / Restrict RDP**: Block TCP 3389 at host/subnet level or allow access only via secure VPN (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\n\n### Phase 2: Credential & Access Reset\n1. **Force Password Resets**: Reset passwords for all administrative and service accounts (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`).\n2. **Revoke Active Sessions**: Terminate all active RDP and PowerShell remoting sessions (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n\n### Phase 3: Eradication & Quarantine (Prefer Quarantine Over Direct Deletion)\n1. **Quarantine Payload**:\n   - Command: Move `C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\svc.exe` to `C:\\\\Quarantine\\\\svc.exe.bak` and restrict ACLs (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`).\n2. **Remove Scheduled Task Persistence**:\n   - Command: `schtasks /Change /TN \"UpdateHelper\" /DISABLE` followed by export an"]
[304.295318, "i", "d removal (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`).\n3. **Remove Registry Run Key Persistence**:\n   - Command: `reg delete \"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Run\" /v \"svc\" /f` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n4. **Remove Service Persistence**:\n   - Command: `sc stop \"svc-helper\"`, `sc config \"svc-helper\" start= disabled`, and move `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` to quarantine (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`).\n\n### Phase 4: System Hardening & Baseline Restoration\n1. **Enable NLA on RDP**:\n   - Set `UserAuthentication = 1` under `HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\Terminal Server\\\\WinStations\\\\RDP-Tcp` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\n2. **Audit Policy Restoration**:\n   - Re-enable audit policies for Account Logon, Process Creation (Event 4688 with command line logging), and Audit Log Clearing (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\n3. **Restore Data from Known-Good Backups**:\n   - Restore encrypted user files (`.locked`) from offline/cloud backups created prior to 2026-08-13 (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`).\n\n### Phase 5: Post-Remediation Verification\n1. Run `schtasks /query` to confirm `UpdateHelper` is gone (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`).\n2. Query `HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Run` to confirm no `svc` entry (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n3. Query `sc query \"svc-helper\"` to confirm service is stopped/removed (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`).\n4. Verify Security Event Log generates new events without truncation or unauthorized clearing (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\nEOF\n"]
