[328.954051, "o", "drwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Aug 16 15:08 \u001b[0m\u001b[01;34m.\u001b[0m\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Aug 16 15:03 \u001b[01;34m..\u001b[0m\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 2856 Aug 16 15:08 baseline-report.md\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1249 Aug 16 15:08 findings.json\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 5359 Aug 16 15:07 intrusion-report.md\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 3382 Aug 16 15:07 progress.md\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 5707 Aug 16 15:08 remediation-plan.md\r\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 2266 Aug 16 15:07 vuln-report.md\r\n"]
[328.954349, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[328.954401, "o", "root@95313cc97448:/app# "]
[329.475723, "i", "head -n 20 /app/progress.md /app/intrusion-report.md /app/vuln-report.md /app/baseline-report.md /app/remediation-plan.md\n"]
[329.4767, "o", "head -n 20 /app/progress.md /app/intrusion-report.md /app/vuln-report.md /app/baseline-report.md /app/remediation-plan.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r==> /app/progress.md <==\r\n# DFIR Investigation Progress and Checklist\r\n\r\n## Target System Information\r\n- Hostname: `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`)\r\n- OS: Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`)\r\n- Analysis Machine Path: `/disk` (Forensic Copy)\r\n- SAS Feed Path: `/sas`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Investigation Checklist & Status\r\n\r\n- [x] Initial Scope & Handoff Review (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`)\r\n- [x] Review Alert Telemetry (`/sas/alerts.json`)\r\n- [x] Review Threat Advisory & CTI (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\r\n- [x] Forensic Analysis of Disk Artifacts:\r\n  - [x] Examine Web Server Logs (`/disk/inetpub/logs/LogFiles/W3SVC1/u_ex.log`)\r\n  - [x] Examine Package Cache Inventory (`/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv`)\r\n  - [x] Examine RDP Configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`)\r\n  - [x] Examine Scheduled Tasks (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`)\r\n\r\n"]
[329.476866, "o", "==> /app/intrusion-report.md <==\r\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Report: Host `rdp-prod-01`  \r\n\r\n## 1. Executive Summary & Attack Chain\r\nAn external threat actor successfully compromised host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) via RDP credential brute forcing. The RDP service was exposed to the internet with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following initial access, the actor established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed a ransomware binary that encrypts files to `.locked` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`), initiated C2 communications and cryptocurrency mining (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`), and cleared the Security Event Log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\r\n\r\nWhile security product alerting (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the ransomware binary, scheduled task, and service, it **failed to detect** the Registry Run key persistence (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) and the cleared Security log (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. MITRE ATT&CK Technique Mapping\r\n\r\n| ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Tactic | Evidence / Finding | Alert Status | Citation |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **T1110** | Brute Force | Credential Access | External RDP brute force attack | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11` |\r\n| **T1021.001** | Remote Desktop Protocol | Lateral Movement | RDP logon allowed without NLA | Alerted | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` |\r\n| **T1059.001** | PowerShell | Execution | Execution of PowerShell post-compromise scripts | Alerted | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` |\r\n| **T1486** | Data Encrypted for Impact | Impact | Ransomware `svc.exe` encrypts user files to `.locked` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |\r\n| **T1053.005** | Scheduled Task | Execution / Persistence | Scheduled task `UpdateHelper` runs `svc.exe` every 5 min | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` |\r\n| **T1547.001** | Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder | Persistence | Run key `svc -> C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\svc.exe` | **SILENT** | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\r\n| **T1543.003** | Windows Service | Persistence | Service `svc-helper` / `svc-helper.sys` installed | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` |\r\n\r\n==> /app/vuln-report.md <==\r\n# Vulnerability Report: Entry Vector Analysis for `rdp-prod-01`  \r\n\r\n## 1. Executive Vulnerability Summary\r\n- **Primary Entry Vector**: Password Brute Force (`T1110`) against RDP (`T1021.001`) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`)\r\n- **Software Vulnerability (CVE) Involvement**: **NONE / Explicit Absence** (`/sas/vulns.json`)\r\n- **Confidence Level**: **HIGH**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Reconciling CVE Claims (CVE-2019-0708 / BlueKeep Evaluation)\r\n\r\nThe initial remediation draft ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`) proposed patching **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**. \r\n\r\nForensic analysis and threat intelligence confirmation demonstrate that **CVE-2019-0708 was NOT exploited** during this incident:\r\n1. **Host OS Version**: The system is running **Windows Server 2022** (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) affects Windows 7, Windows Server 2008 R2, and Windows Server 2008. Windows Server 2022 is not vulnerable to BlueKeep.\r\n2. **Vulnerability Feed**: The vulnerability scan report at `/sas/vulns.json` contains an empty list `[]`, indicating no software vulnerabilities were flagged by the security product.\r\n3. **Threat Intelligence Mapping**: The threat advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`) attributes the initial entry step explicitly to **T1110 (Brute Force)** via RDP logon, rather than remote code execution exploit payloads.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n==> /app/baseline-report.md <==\r\n# Configuration Baseline Weaknesses Report: `rdp-prod-01`  \r\n\r\n## 1. Executive Summary\r\nAn evaluation of configuration baselines on host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) revealed multiple critical baseline security gaps that facilitated initial intrusion, persistence, and an"]
[329.477244, "o", "ti-forensics. The primary weakness is an insecure Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) baseline flagged in check `CHK-06` (`/sas/baseline.json:3`).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Identified Baseline Weaknesses & Evidence\r\n\r\n### 1. RDP Network Level Authentication (NLA) Disabled (`CHK-06` / `BAS-01`)\r\n- **Finding**: RDP configuration file `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg` explicitly records `UserAuthentication = 0 (NLA disabled), connections allowed` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\r\n- **Telemetry Reference**: Flagged in SAS baseline telemetry check `CHK-06` (`/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:26`).\r\n- **Impact**: Disabling NLA allows unauthenticated clients to establish RDP sessions and perform brute-force attacks against the Windows logon interface without authenticating at the network layer first.\r\n\r\n### 2. Direct Internet Exposure of Management Services\r\n- **Finding**: RDP (TCP port 3389) was directly exposed to public IP addresses including threat origin IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).\r\n- **Impact**: Unrestricted exposure of remote administration interfaces invites automated password spraying and brute-forcing (`T1110`).\r\n\r\n### 3. Account Security & Password Policy Weakness\r\n- **Finding**: Administrative accounts were susceptible to automated credential brute forcing (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11`).\r\n\r\n==> /app/remediation-plan.md <==\r\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan: Host `rdp-prod-01`  \r\n\r\n## 1. Plan Overview & Principles\r\nThis remediation plan outlines containment, eradication, baseline hardening, and recovery actions for host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). In accordance with incident response rules:\r\n- **Quarantine / Backup Over Deletion**: Malware samples, persistence artifacts, and modified configurations are backed up or quarantined rather than immediately deleted to preserve evidence.\r\n- **Evidence-Based Actions**: Every action is mapped directly to forensic evidence from `/disk` or `/sas`.\r\n- **Change Ticket Reconciliation**: Reconciles draft ticket `CHG-9792` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-9792\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target / Location | Status | Rationale & Evidence | Citation |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **1** | Block inbound network traffic | IP `198.51.100.92` | **PROPOSED** | Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with confirmed threat actor IP `198.51.100.92`. | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` |\r\n| **2** | Enable NLA & Harden RDP | TCP Port 3389 / RDP | **PROPOSED** | Entry was via RDP password brute force (`T1110`), enabled by NLA being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`). Corrected from invalid BlueKeep claim. | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4` |\r\n| **3** | Cancel cron miner removal | `/var/spool/cron/root` | **REJECTED** | Target host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`); Linux cron miner was a stale/erroneous draft entry. | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\r\n| **4** | Quarantine ransomware binary | `/Users/Public/svc.exe` | **TODO** | Move `svc.exe` (`4f8a5c4380a18bca293c7e9130caf957973cc733e9b2c32c2e5240aa9e2c2dae`) to secure forensic quarantine folder. | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |\r\n| **5** | Disable & Quarantine Scheduled Task | `/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` | **TODO** | Backup task definition XML and remove `UpdateHelper` task that executes `svc.exe` every 5 minutes. | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` |\r\n| **6** | Quarantine Registry Run Key | `/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` | **TODO** | Delete Registry Run value `svc -> C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\svc.exe` under `HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Run`. (**Silent finding**) | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\r\n"]
